window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-42acd5332ef4d7e7"]={"key":"ny_b1-42acd5332ef4d7e7","group":"ny_b1","uid":"42acd5332ef4d7e7","rank":96,"title":"saltmarsh clip usage note stateful 01","occupation":"film_video_editors","archetype":"supplied_source","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are preparing the payout documentation for Saltmarsh Footage Co-op after Priya Ekwueme told us that the licensing export has been used for years without anyone writing down what its columns actually mean. Bertrand Quill is taking over this year's run and will be working without Priya available to interpret an edit, a licence line, or a pack sale, so I need a plain-language usage-counting note that he can apply consistently and then hand to Finance with confidence. Use the supplied workbook `saltmarsh_usage_register.xlsx` as the complete source for this work. It contains the opening usage position, subsequent usage-related events, and the payout information needed for the examples; do not look up current rates, contributor details, or licensing practice elsewhere. The workbook is an operational export rather than a polished data dictionary: some fields are absent, the same time field is not presented consistently, there is material beside the main register that is not part of the usage ledger, and one old calculated field is still populated even though it no longer represents the live count. Treat the source as something you must inspect and interpret rather than as instructions about how the count should work. Please write `clip_usage_counting_note.xlsx` into the top level of the working directory where you start, using exactly that filename. The file should be usable as a short internal handover, not as a data dump: include a clear plain-language explanation of what counts as a clip use, how the opening position is carried forward, how later events change it, how to recognise a licence that does not itself establish a use, how to handle a re-cut or repeated appearance of the same shot, and how a sale containing several clips affects each clip's count. Explain how you treated records whose dates or times cannot be established confidently and fields that are missing, and make the treatment visible enough that Bertrand can repeat it rather than silently guessing. Include worked payout examples based only on records in `saltmarsh_usage_register.xlsx`, with enough identifiers and intermediate reasoning for another person to reproduce the result; use at least one ordinary single-clip example and examples that expose the licence-only, re-cut, and multi-clip-pack distinctions. Where the source supports a contributor-level payout, show how the applicable usage figure connects to the supplied payout information, while leaving any unsupported amount or attribution unresolved instead of inventing it. The note should call out the source fields you relied on and identify the stale helper field and the unrelated material so that a future user does not accidentally use either. Please preserve the source workbook as an input and do not overwrite it, embed a replacement copy of the raw register, or add a second deliverable. Keep the note concise enough to read before a payout run, but do not omit a limitation merely to make it shorter. Use the names and labels from the supplied material where they are needed, distinguish facts taken from the workbook from your interpretation, and make the final document professional enough for Helena Yamamoto, Wilhelmina Hendricks, Xiomara Dimitrov, Iris Mortensen, or Estelle Bruns to review on behalf of the business without needing a meeting with Priya.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/saltmarsh_usage_register.xlsx` — Complete supplied source containing the opening usage state, later usage events, payout information, and unrelated operational material needed to construct and verify the usage-counting note.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `clip_usage_counting_note.xlsx` — A concise, plain-language internal usage-counting note with source interpretation, explicit assumptions and exclusions, replay logic, and worked payout examples. (Write the file at the top level of the starting working directory using exactly the specified filename.; Use only facts and payout information supported by the supplied workbook.; Do not overwrite or embed a replacement copy of the source register.; Make treatment of ambiguity, missing fields, licence-only records, re-cuts, multi-clip packs, the stale helper field, and the unrelated table explicit.; Include reproducible intermediate reasoning in the worked examples and leave unsupported amounts or attributions unresolved rather than inventing them.; The result must be readable by a finance officer who has not worked on an edit timeline.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/saltmarsh_usage_register.xlsx","bytes":7164,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/ed1bc5d6b951cf5e4861d3843b90f604437d291493b734a0d3f0a61acb298b97.xlsx","sha256":"ed1bc5d6b951cf5e4861d3843b90f604437d291493b734a0d3f0a61acb298b97","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Usage export","row_count":16,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Saltmarsh Footage Co-op | Licensing usage export"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Opening state + subsequent usage-related events; exported 2026-08-20 09:15 UTC"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Clip ID","Contributor ID","Opening Uses","Event ID","Event Type","Event Date/Time","Transaction / Licence ID","Clip IDs in Pack","Shot / Use Key","Delivery / Status","Notes","Retired Usage Helper","","Payout reference (source)","","","","Unrelated operations table"]},{"r":"5","cells":["C-101","CON-ALP","2","OPEN-101","OPENING","45658","","","","Opening position","As at opening date","4","","Contributor ID","Contributor label","Rate per counted use","Currency","Archive\nbox","Owner"]},{"r":"6","cells":["C-102","CON-BRN","0","OPEN-102","OPENING","45658","","","","Opening position","As at opening date","0","","CON-ALP","Aster Lane","85","USD","BX-17","Iris Mortensen"]},{"r":"7","cells":["C-103","CON-CED","1","OPEN-103","OPENING","45658","","","","Opening position","As at opening date","3","","CON-BRN","Briar North","100","USD","BX-18","Estelle Bruns"]},{"r":"8","cells":["C-104","CON-DEN","3","OPEN-104","OPENING","45658","","","","Opening position","As at opening date","4","","CON-CED","Cedar Vale","75","USD"]},{"r":"9","cells":["C-105","CON-EVE","4","OPEN-105","OPENING","45658","","","","Opening position","No later event in export","4"]},{"r":"10","cells":["C-101","CON-ALP","","E-201","SINGLE_CLIP_USE","45700.60416666666","TX-501","","SK-101-A","Delivered","First cut supplied","4","","CON-DEN","Denton Field","60","USD"]},{"r":"11","cells":["C-101","CON-ALP","","E-202","LICENCE_ONLY","2025-02-18 08:00","LIC-88","","","Permission only","Availability / permission; no delivery recorded","4"]},{"r":"12","cells":["C-101","CON-ALP","","E-203","EDIT_RECUT","03/04/2025","TX-501","","SK-101-A","Delivered in revised cut","Same underlying shot/use key as E-201","4"]},{"r":"13","cells":["C-102","CON-BRN","","E-204","PACK_SALE","45736.41666666666","TX-PACK-77","C-102|C-103|C-104","SK-102-P","Pack delivered","One identifiable line for C-102 in pack","0"]},{"r":"14","cells":["C-103","CON-CED","","E-205","PACK_SALE","45736.41666666666","TX-PACK-77","C-102|C-103|C-104","SK-103-P","Pack delivered","One identifiable line for C-103 in pack","3"]},{"r":"15","cells":["C-104","CON-DEN","","E-206","PACK_SALE","45736.41666666666","TX-PACK-77","C-102|C-103|C-104","SK-104-P","Pack delivered","One identifiable line for C-104 in pack","4"]},{"r":"16","cells":["C-104","","","E-207","SINGLE_CLIP_USE","04/05/2025","","","SK-104-B","Delivered","Clip linked, but date format is ambiguous and contributor field is blank","4"]},{"r":"17","cells":["C-103","CON-CED","","E-208","LICENCE_ONLY","2025-04-12 11:00","LIC-91","","","Permission only","Licence record without delivery evidence","3"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/clip_usage_counting_note.xlsx","bytes":8344,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/d4b0e7874b92239b2b0ed32b710ecb6b06816f8ae3c39b612fab928f87de828f.xlsx","sha256":"d4b0e7874b92239b2b0ed32b710ecb6b06816f8ae3c39b612fab928f87de828f","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Counting note","row_count":23,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Saltmarsh Footage Co-op | Clip usage counting note"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Internal handover for Bertrand Quill | prepared for Finance review | version 1"]},{"r":"3","cells":[]},{"r":"4","cells":["1. Scope and source facts"]},{"r":"5","cells":["[SOURCE FACT] Sole source: saltmarsh_usage_register.xlsx (sheet “Usage export”). This note interprets that operational export; it does not replace or reproduce the register."]},{"r":"6","cells":["[SOURCE FACT] The live register fields used are Clip ID, Contributor ID, Opening Uses, Event ID, Event Type, Event Date/Time, Transaction / Licence ID, Clip IDs in Pack, Shot / Use Key, Delivery / Status, and Notes. The payout table supplies Contributor ID, Contributor label, Rate per counted use, and Currency."]},{"r":"7","cells":["[SOURCE FACT] The beside-table headed “Unrelated operations table” contains “Archive\nbox” and “Owner” (the line break is part of that header) plus BX-17/BX-18 assignments. It is out of scope and must not be read as usage data."]},{"r":"8","cells":["[RULE] A clip use is one identifiable appearance/delivery of a clip in a delivered edit or sale, counted once per underlying use. A licensing permission, availability record, or administrative transaction is not itself a use. Keep clip usage, contributor attribution, and money as separate steps."]},{"r":"9","cells":["2. Replay method (the repeatable calculation)"]},{"r":"10","cells":["1) Start each Clip ID at its Opening Uses value. Do not recompute the opening position from current event rows. 2) Review current rows by Event ID. Add one only for a supported, countable delivered use. 3) Use Clip ID + Shot / Use Key + Transaction / Licence ID + Notes to link rows that describe the same underlying use; deduplicate linked re-cuts. 4) For a pack transaction, allocate at clip level: each identifiable clip line is one use for that clip. 5) Roll a clip result to a contributor only when the source supplies the linkage; then multiply by that contributor’s supplied rate."]},{"r":"11","cells":["[EXCLUSION] Retired Usage Helper is a stale helper column, not a live input. It conflicts with replayed values (for example C-101 helper 4 versus replay 3; C-102 helper 0 versus replay 1). Using it would carry an obsolete count into payout."]},{"r":"12","cells":["[ASSUMPTION / TIMING] Event Date/Time mixes true spreadsheet datetimes (for example E-201 and E-204), ISO-like text (E-202 and E-208), and slash-form text that is ambiguous without a day/month convention (E-203 “03/04/2025”; E-207 “04/05/2025”). Use clear dates for ordering. Do not invent a convention for slash dates. If identity/status makes a slash-dated row a duplicate of a known use, it may be linked for deduplication; a unique slash-dated use is held out of the count until confirmed."]},{"r":"13","cells":["[MISSING FIELDS] Blank values are not silently filled. E-207 has no Contributor ID or transaction ID and an ambiguous date; hold it, record the reason, and ask the source owner/Finance to confirm the date, delivery, and attribution before payment. A clear clip-level opening linkage can support a provisional contributor roll-up only for already countable events; it cannot cure an unresolved event."]},{"r":"14","cells":["3. Worked examples and payout arithmetic"]},{"r":"15","cells":["Clip / source identifiers","Opening","Event replay (included or excluded)","Final usage","Supplied payout connection"]},{"r":"16","cells":["C-101 | contributor CON-ALP | helper 4","2","+1 E-201 / TX-501 / SK-101-A (delivered single-clip use); +0 E-202 / LIC-88 (licence-only); +0 E-203 / TX-501 / SK-101-A (re-cut of same use, slash date linked as duplicate)","2 + 1 = 3","CON-ALP rate = $85 USD/use. 3 × $85 = $255 USD. Helper 4 is ignored."]},{"r":"17","cells":["C-102 | contributor CON-BRN","0","+1 E-204 / TX-PACK-77. Pack row names C-102|C-103|C-104; this is the C-102 line.","0 + 1 = 1","CON-BRN rate = $100 USD/use. 1 × $100 = $100 USD. The pack transaction is not one use of every clip."]},{"r":"18","cells":["C-103 | contributor CON-CED | helper 3","1","+1 E-205 / TX-PACK-77 (the identifiable C-103 line); +0 E-208 / LIC-91 (licence-only).","1 + 1 = 2","CON-CED rate = $75 USD/use. 2 × $75 = $150 USD. Helper 3 is ignored."]},{"r":"19","cells":["C-104 | contributor CON-DEN | helper 4","3","+1 E-206 / TX-PACK-77 (the identifiable C-104 line); +0 E-207 / SK-104-B (unique delivery claim, but slash date “04/05/2025”, blank Contributor ID and blank transaction ID: held pending confirmation).","3 + 1 = 4 current count; E-207 excluded","CON-DEN rate = $60 USD/use. Current supported payout = 4 × $60 = $240 USD. If E-207 is later confirmed, add one use and resolve attribution before any extra $60 is paid."]},{"r":"20","cells":["C-105 | contributor CON-EVE","4","No later event row in the export.","4 + 0 = 4","No new payout arithmetic is needed; opening use position carries forward."]},{"r":"21","cells":["4. Operator checklist before sending to Finance"]},{"r":"22","cells":["• Filter to the primary register columns A:L in “Usage export”; ignore the beside-table.\n• For each clip, write opening count, then list included event IDs and one-line reasons for exclusions or deduplication.\n• Verify every included event has delivery evidence and a usable identity. Do not count every licensing export row.\n• For packs, reconcile transaction-level TX-PACK-77 to the clip-level lines E-204, E-205 and E-206.\n• Recheck mixed/ambiguous times and blanks. Hold unresolved rows and escalate; do not guess.\n• Apply the payout rate only after clip usage and contributor linkage are established. Keep any unsupported attribution or amount unresolved."]},{"r":"23","cells":["[LIMITATION] This note states a source-grounded operating convention, not an external licensing rule. The source does not supply a day/month convention for slash dates or a complete approval trail for E-207; Finance must resolve those items before changing the count."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted workbook exists at the required top-level filename and opens as a valid spreadsheet.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Filesystem location and workbook parseability.","grader_hint":"Check the exact filename and top-level placement, then open it with a standard spreadsheet library."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The note is readable as a professional handover for a finance officer with no edit-timeline expertise.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered workbook prose and examples.","grader_hint":"Judge whether terminology is explained plainly and whether a new operator could use the note without a meeting."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The note identifies `saltmarsh_usage_register.xlsx` as its sole source.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source statement in the delivered workbook.","grader_hint":"Search extracted text for the exact source filename."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The opening usage position is treated as the starting state rather than recomputed from later events alone.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Method explanation and at least one worked example.","grader_hint":"Verify the note explicitly carries forward an opening count and shows it in an example."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Final clip usage equals the opening count plus only the current events the note classifies as countable, with each underlying use represented once.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Method and examples compared with source replay.","grader_hint":"Recalculate several clips from the source and compare the stated treatment and totals."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The note defines a clip use in operational language that a non-editor can apply.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definition section or equivalent prose.","grader_hint":"Require a practical distinction between a counted use and a mere administrative or permission record."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Licence-only records do not increase clip usage unless the source separately supports a countable use.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rule and licence-only worked example.","grader_hint":"Trace the cited licence-only source row and confirm the final count excludes it."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The note explains why a licence and a use are different concepts.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Plain-language explanation.","grader_hint":"Look for an explanation understandable without licensing jargon."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A re-cut or repeated appearance of the same underlying shot is not automatically counted as a second use.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rule and source-linked example.","grader_hint":"Compare the note's treatment with the related event rows and ensure it does not blindly add both."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The note gives a defensible operational test for recognising a re-cut or repeated appearance.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Editorial interpretation section.","grader_hint":"Judge whether another analyst could apply the stated test consistently to the supplied rows."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A multi-clip pack sale is not treated as one use of every clip, and the note explains the clip-level allocation supported by the source.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pack-sale rule and worked example.","grader_hint":"Verify that the example distinguishes the pack transaction from the individual clips it contains."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The pack-sale explanation is understandable to a payout operator and does not rely on unexplained editing terminology.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worked example prose.","grader_hint":"Assess practical usability, not merely presence of the word pack."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The note distinguishes a transaction-level event from the clip-level usage outcome.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Method and examples.","grader_hint":"Confirm the transformation is described at both levels."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The stale retired helper column is explicitly identified and excluded from the live calculation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source-field discussion and calculation examples.","grader_hint":"Match the named helper column to the source and confirm the note uses replayed values instead."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The note explains why the retired helper column is unsafe rather than merely saying not to use it.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Method note.","grader_hint":"Look for a reference to stale or conflicting values and the consequence for payouts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The mixed date/time representations are noticed and described.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Data-quality discussion.","grader_hint":"Compare the note with the actual mixed representations in the source column."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The note states a consistent, defensible treatment for the ambiguous date/time representation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Assumptions or exception treatment.","grader_hint":"Accept a defensible disclosed convention or exclusion; do not require a particular convention unless supported by the source."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The treatment of an event affected by ambiguous timing is applied consistently in the worked result.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source-linked example and final count.","grader_hint":"Trace the ambiguous row and verify the example follows the disclosed treatment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Missing fields are acknowledged and the note states when a missing value is excluded, assumed, or left unresolved.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Limitations and assumptions section.","grader_hint":"Require visible treatment, not silent filling."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"No unsupported contributor, clip, event, date, or payout fact is invented.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Full workbook compared with source.","grader_hint":"Check every factual claim in examples and payout statements against the supplied workbook."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each worked example cites enough source identifiers to locate the relevant clip and event rows.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Examples.","grader_hint":"Require clip or transaction identifiers and not just generic descriptions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"At least one worked example shows an ordinary single-clip use increasing the count from its opening state.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worked example arithmetic.","grader_hint":"Verify opening count, included event, and resulting count."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"At least one worked example shows a licence-only event leaving the count unchanged.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worked example arithmetic.","grader_hint":"Confirm the cited source event is licence-only."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"At least one worked example shows the re-cut or repeated shot not being added twice.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worked example arithmetic.","grader_hint":"Check the source's related editorial rows and the note's single-use result."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"At least one worked example shows how a pack sale affects multiple clips at clip level.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worked example arithmetic.","grader_hint":"Require separate clip outcomes rather than one undifferentiated pack count."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Worked examples display intermediate arithmetic sufficient to reproduce each final usage result.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Example tables or prose.","grader_hint":"Look for opening value, included or excluded events, adjustments, and resulting value."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The payout examples use the supplied payout basis or rate and do not substitute an external rate.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Payout examples compared with payout reference.","grader_hint":"Recalculate the example using only the source payout information."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Where payout attribution is unsupported by the source, the note leaves it unresolved or clearly labels the limitation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Payout limitation statements.","grader_hint":"Check unresolved cases against missing source fields."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every numeric payout example agrees with the source-derived usage and payout arithmetic within ±$0.01.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Example calculations and source replay.","grader_hint":"Recompute each displayed monetary example using the source rate and stated usage."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The note does not use the stale helper values where the current replay produces different results.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Examples and method.","grader_hint":"Compare displayed results with both the helper field and independent replay."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The note identifies the unrelated beside-table material as out of scope for usage counting.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source-scope statement.","grader_hint":"Match the described material to the side table on the source sheet."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The line-break-containing header is treated as a header belonging to the unrelated table and not misread as a usage field.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Field inventory or scope explanation.","grader_hint":"Inspect extracted cell text and the note's identification of the side table."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The note separates source facts, calculation rules, assumptions, and unresolved limitations.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall organization and wording.","grader_hint":"Judge whether a reviewer can tell what came from the workbook versus what the author decided."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The note names the live source fields used for the count and payout calculation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Field inventory.","grader_hint":"Compare named fields with the actual primary register and payout reference."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The note explains how event identity is used to avoid counting the same underlying use more than once.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Method explanation.","grader_hint":"Require a practical identity or linkage concept grounded in supplied fields."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The final usage treatment is consistent across the clips used in the examples.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-example comparison.","grader_hint":"Check that the note does not apply contradictory definitions to similar event types."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delivered workbook contains a plain-language note and worked examples rather than only raw source data.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook contents.","grader_hint":"Inspect rendered sheets and extracted text for substantive prose and examples."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The source workbook is not overwritten, altered, or embedded as a replacement raw register in the deliverable.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison with supplied source and deliverable structure.","grader_hint":"Ensure the deliverable is a note, not a copied raw register, and the original source remains available."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delivered workbook contains no `#REF!`, `#DIV/0!`, or `#VALUE!` strings or formula errors.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook formula and text scan.","grader_hint":"Scan formulas, cached values, and extracted text for all three error tokens."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The examples and instructions are concise enough for use before a payout run while retaining material caveats.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered workbook.","grader_hint":"Judge practical length, scanability, and whether brevity has removed a decision-critical limitation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The note gives a concrete next action for a record that cannot be resolved from the source.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exception-handling prose.","grader_hint":"Require an actionable hold, review, or escalation treatment without inventing data."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The note preserves the distinction between clip usage, contributor attribution, and monetary payout.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definitions and payout examples.","grader_hint":"Verify that a clip count is not presented as a payout amount unless the supplied basis supports the conversion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A second analyst could reproduce the worked examples and identify where judgment entered the calculation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Complete delivered workbook.","grader_hint":"Perform an independent replay from the source using only the note and assess whether the decisions are discoverable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The note does not claim that every licensing export row is a use.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definition and scope statements.","grader_hint":"Check the prose and examples for explicit or implicit overcounting."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The note states how the final clip-level result rolls up to a contributor only when the source supplies the necessary linkage.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Contributor payout explanation.","grader_hint":"Compare rollups with contributor identifiers and flag unsupported aggregation claims."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The delivered artifact is professionally usable, with clear labels, legible calculations, and no distracting raw-data clutter.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered spreadsheet.","grader_hint":"Assess usability for the named finance handover, including legibility and navigation."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Saltmarsh Footage Co-op pays contributor filmmakers from clip-usage figures, and its finance process is moving from Priya Ekwueme's operational knowledge to an independently usable payout note. The note will be used by Bertrand Quill in a high-stakes contributor payment run involving records associated with Foxglove Studios and the Limeworth Regional Office.","difficulty_sources":["The supplied workbook contains an opening usage state and subsequent licensing and editorial events that must be replayed into a defensible final usage position.","Usage concepts are easy to confuse: a licence record is not automatically a use, a re-cut of the same shot does not necessarily create another use, and a multi-clip pack sale cannot be treated as one use of every clip.","Some source fields are absent, one time column mixes representations including an ambiguous representation, and a retired helper column contains stale values.","The output must translate editorial concepts into plain language for a finance officer who will run contributor payouts without supervision."],"authoring_plan":{"source_design":{"artifact":"saltmarsh_usage_register.xlsx","semantic_sources":[{"name":"opening usage state","purpose":"Provide the initial per-clip usage position and contributor linkage as of the opening date."},{"name":"usage event ledger","purpose":"Provide subsequent licensing, editorial, and pack-sale events that must be replayed against the opening state."},{"name":"payout reference","purpose":"Provide the supplied payout basis or rate information needed for worked examples."}],"layout":"Use a single workbook with a primary register and supporting source material. Put an unrelated small table beside the primary register on the same sheet, and include a line break inside one of that unrelated table's header strings. The build should remain text-extractable and internally consistent.","seeded_defects_exactly":["Within one date/time column of the primary register, mix at least two representations, including one representation that is genuinely ambiguous without an explicit interpretation.","Place a second unrelated table beside the real usage table on the same sheet; embed a line break in one header string of the unrelated table.","Include a retired helper column with stale values that conflict with at least some values obtained by replaying the opening state and current events."],"do_not_seed":["No other standard layout defects or formula errors.","No fabricated external facts, live rates, real personal identifiers, or unsupported payout rules.","Do not include a governing rulebook that resolves the counting judgments for the solver."]},"state_and_events":{"opening_state":"Include several clips with contributor identifiers and opening use counts, including at least one clip that later receives events and one that remains unchanged.","event_categories":["A licence-only record that establishes permission or availability but does not by itself establish a delivered or counted use.","A normal single-clip use that should increase the relevant clip's count.","A re-cut or repeated appearance of the same underlying shot that tests whether the same use is being counted twice.","A pack sale containing several identifiable clips, requiring the solver to determine the clip-level treatment rather than counting the pack as one use for all clips.","At least one event with a missing field whose treatment must be stated.","At least one event affected by the mixed and ambiguous date/time representation."],"intended_stateful_rule":"The gold is derived by replaying current, countable events against the opening state, with each underlying counted clip use represented once, licence-only events excluded from use totals, repeated editorial treatment of the same use not double-counted, and a multi-clip pack allocated at clip level according to the evidence in the source. The note must disclose any defensible treatment selected for ambiguous or incomplete records.","payout_relationship":"For each worked example, the stated usage result must be traceable from opening count plus included event effects, then connected to the supplied payout basis without using the retired helper column."},"gold_derivation":{"method":"Use a small offline script or equivalent independently reviewed calculation to replay the opening state and event ledger. Derive expected final clip counts, contributor rollups where supported, and example payout arithmetic from the source data rather than hard-coding values.","review_focus":["Confirm every graded fact is text-extractable from the workbook.","Confirm the stale helper values are not needed to derive the intended result.","Confirm the ambiguity is material but has at least one defensible, disclosed treatment.","Confirm the worked examples can be reproduced from source identifiers and visible intermediate facts."]}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"multi_artifact_bundle","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"usage_register_workbook","filename":"saltmarsh_usage_register.xlsx","purpose":"Complete supplied source containing the opening usage state, later usage events, payout information, and unrelated operational material needed to construct and verify the usage-counting note.","required":true,"discovery":"Open the workbook from the top level of the working directory; inspect all visible tables and fields before drafting the note."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"clip_usage_counting_note","filename":"clip_usage_counting_note.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"A concise, plain-language internal usage-counting note with source interpretation, explicit assumptions and exclusions, replay logic, and worked payout examples.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file at the top level of the starting working directory using exactly the specified filename.","Use only facts and payout information supported by the supplied workbook.","Do not overwrite or embed a replacement copy of the source register.","Make treatment of ambiguity, missing fields, licence-only records, re-cuts, multi-clip packs, the stale helper field, and the unrelated table explicit.","Include reproducible intermediate reasoning in the worked examples and leave unsupported amounts or attributions unresolved rather than inventing them.","The result must be readable by a finance officer who has not worked on an edit timeline."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"inspect_quality","work_product":"media_edit","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"supplied_source@v4","occupation":"film_video_editors","sector":"information","task_archetype":"supplied_source","estimated_professional_hours":3.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Build the source and an independently replayed reference solution offline, then have a domain-aware reviewer inspect the note for defensible interpretation, completeness, and usability against the supplied workbook.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["Some ambiguity-related criteria permit more than one defensible treatment, provided the treatment is consistent, source-grounded, and disclosed.","The spreadsheet renderer may display line breaks differently from extracted cell text, so the side-table defect should be verified both structurally and through workbook inspection."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:25:52+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:25:52+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:25:52+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:25:52+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R09']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:25:52+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/42acd5332ef4d7e7","declared_deliverables":["clip_usage_counting_note.xlsx"]};
